v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application, replacing a five-file
browser prototype that was reviewed on 2026-09-28 and found not releasable (eight reproduced
functional defects plus a credential published in a document).

v2.1.0 added a Tie bet alongside Banker or Player on the same hand, moved the disclaimer to the foot
of the window, and removed page scrolling. v2.2.0 put Hand History, Statistics and Bankroll beside
the betting column so the module works at half screen width, gave the bead plate a fixed 10 x 10 box
of 100 colour-only hands, and renamed the two table panels. v2.2.1 shrank the dots to 14px and
corrected the fill order to top-to-bottom then left-to-right.

v2.3.0 made PASS record the table's result: passing opens the hand with nothing at risk, the result
feeds Hand History, the result distribution and the streaks, and the bankroll never moves.

v2.4.0 gives the Tie insurance its own stake, set independently of the main bet, with each bet button
showing the stake it will place: Banker 100u with a 10u Tie insurance nets +$425 when Banker wins,
+$400 when the Tie lands and -$550 when Player wins, at $5 per unit.

